            <ArticleTitle>Intranasal fentanyl for analgesia in the paediatric emergency department.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/emj.2008.070474</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intranasal opiate analgesia is the first choice in children presenting to paediatric emergency departments with severe pain. A prospective observational study was performed which showed that intranasal fentanyl is a safe effective alternative to diamorphine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
